DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The DTrace uuddpp provider allows users to trace events in the udp(4) proto‐
     col implementation.  The uuddpp::::::sseenndd() probe fires whenever the kernel
     prepares to transmit a UDP packet, and the uuddpp::::::rreecceeiivvee() probe fires
     whenever the kernel receives a UDP packet, unless the UDP header is in‐
     complete, the destination port is 0, the length field is invalid, or the
     checksum is wrong.  The arguments to these probes can be used to obtain
     detailed information about the IP and UDP headers of the corresponding
     packet.

